key. If that entry was malformed, the helper rejected an envelope, even when a later entry held a valid signature from the same key. DSSE treats the key ID as an unauthenticated hint, so the helper also rejected a valid signature under a different key ID. The key-pinned sigstore path already tries each entry.\n\nThe helper now does the same: it returns the decoded payload when any entry verifies, and the same errors as before when none does.\n\n2 new regression tests cover both cases. Each test envelope also goes through the dsse crate, added as a dev-dependency, so the tests fail if the helper and a separate DSSE verifier disagree. The format, clippy and test steps from the CI workflow pass with all features and with default features off.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * DSSE envelope verification now checks all signatures matching the supplied key, so an invalid extra signature does not prevent a valid signature from verifying.\n  * Key ID matching is case-insensitive. Verification reports an error appropriate to whether matching signature entries are absent, malformed, or invalid.\n  * Changing the payload type still causes verification to fail.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-30T22:49:34Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T23:14:36Z","closed_at":"2026-09-30T23:14:36Z","merged_at":"2026-09-30T23:14:36Z","merge_commit_sha":"a1e72765852cca0de7a3f5fbe68aab3aad74074f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"astrogilda-forks:fix/dsse-helper-try-every-signature-0930","ref":"fix/dsse-helper-try-every-signature-0930","repo":{"id":1398595301,"node_id":"R_kgDOU1ze5Q","name":"packslip","full_name":"astrogilda-forks/packslip","owner":{"login":"astrogilda-forks","id":335228044,"node_id":"O_kgDOE_ssjA","avatar_url":"h